{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/199320-let-s-talk-doctrine-agenda-subgroupings-discussion","id":199320,"title":"Let's Talk Doctrine - Agenda Subgroupings Discussion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-16T15:13:33-07:00","id":199320,"title":"Let's Talk Doctrine - Agenda Subgroupings Discussion","content":"One of the things from Flowers that I found interesting to read up on was the various schools of thought within the Agendas; ergo, this thread.<br /> <br /> It's curious, in a way, how a fair few of those subgroupings seem to evoke other Agendas \u2014 the Nation of Hell and the theo-separatists, for example, have pretty clear common cause with the Tempters, and the celestial insurgency seems like the group of Integrators the Saboteurs would find the most palatable. Meanwhile, the Integrators seem to be the only Agenda without a major faction whose operative thought includes &quot;seeking the Agenda's mainstream Hell is futile.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm having a little trouble getting a feel for what the hermetics' aim is; near as I can tell they're vaguely Inquisitor-esque in their approach to the Hell of the Builders insofar as I can piece together their beliefs from their typical structure and the individuals whose wisdom is given as examples the mystics follow \u2014 Isis's name means &quot;Throne&quot; and she's the protector of the humaniform deity who presides over the canopic jar that holds the liver; Hermes Trismegistus is credited with the knowledge of alchemy, astronomy, and theurgy; and a cursory wikiing of Sufiism suggests a purification of the inner self is a major focus. My current takeaway is that the hermetics aim to make the location of their Hell &quot;wherever I am&quot; or at least discover reliable means of occulting people, places, and things from the sight of God. Anybody have any thoughts on this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T21:31:37-07:00","id":200705,"title":"","content":"Tempters embrace being human. For most this means wealth, power or personal enjoyment, the things that humans covet and that make them feel like more, if only superficially. Hermetics embrace the spiritual inclinations of humans; they emphasize the gnostic aspects of the setting and humanity's Seeker archetype.<br /> <br /> Think of them as Twilight Sparkle, as opposed to most other Tempters leaning towards Rarity or Pinkie Pie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T21:40:44-07:00","id":200726,"title":"","content":"See, I <i>get</i> that. I'm having trouble understanding it as a philosophy <i>on Hell as an achievable state.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T02:48:34-07:00","id":200964,"title":"","content":"Could you elaborate?<br /> <br /> It seems simple enough to me; Humanity is clever. Clever enough that they had a name for what we seek before we Fell. Somewhere, in amidst all the Wisdom and accumulated learning they may have found Hell. It's less 'Hell is where I am' and more &quot;Hell is here, somewhere and they can help me find it/rebuild it&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Hermetics don't nessicarily belive that Hell is a believable state of mind/soul or an enlightened wisdom, (though they can). That there is Inquisitor talk, (and neatly covers a concept I once had). The slightly more fun way to run them is that they believe Hell <i>has already been achieved</i>. They are looking for something that already exists and, whatever the individual motivations are using people to help get them there, or maybe just take those humans with them.<br /> <br /> Look at it this way; when trying to find a spiritual location what kind of map do you use? And if you can find the mapmakers, or at least his/her distant family and you could convince them to help, why wouldn't you? Take, for example, if you we're looking for the Hedge but you haven't met a changeling, maybe you haven't even heard of them. What about the Hisil/Shadow World, but werewolves are just in the movies and are horribly cursed.<br /> Remember, for a long time the line for priest and magician was pretty thin. Even with Christianity, the line can be a might fuzzy to those who aren't properly schooled, (eg. Saints).<br /> <br /> It is not like we aren't already given the impression that the G-M is more limited in other worlds anyway. Even if this is only briefly observed...it could inspire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T10:01:58-07:00","id":201232,"title":"","content":"Except that &quot;Hell is already here&quot; and &quot;Hell can be built on Earth or found in other worlds&quot; describes the views of the aesthetes and the constructivists.<br /> <br /> One can look at Prometheus theory and see how that rationale works \u2014 create Hell by bringing humanity to awareness of the Machine so that they then make it impossible for Its plans to retain any hold on the world, which feeds nicely into the Builders' penchant for catspaws and intermediaries \u2014 and the other two major strains of Tempter philosophy are straightforward in their definitions of Hell.<br /> <br /> The mystics don't have such a clear view of the thing; the main hints we have are &quot;they believe Hell can be found in 'the wisdom of humanity'&quot; and &quot;they often organize their associations into an initiatory cult-esque form.&quot; It's not a lot to go on.<br /> <br /> ETA: I suppose, given the degreed structure of such cults and the nature of Prometheus theory, that the mystics conceive of Hell as an assembly of demons - the wordplayer in me sees some appeal in the being an Inner Circle of Hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-18-2014, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T23:18:22-07:00","id":203564,"title":"","content":"A little more looking into Sufism and the cults of Isis and Hermes Trismegistus suggests another possibility: the creation of Hell by developing the means to trick the Machine into seeing a place or thing as already spoken for in its plans and thus not to be tampered with.<br /> <br /> This is terribly vexing. Any of the writers care to chime in with a clarification?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}